+# M4 failure and recovery inventory
+
+Source baseline: `68c72d4` (HEAD observed 2026-11-02). Read-only source research; no builds, test execution, network, GUI, user configuration, credentials, local models, or audio were accessed. This document is the only authored artifact. Scope is the five pipeline stages, errors they receive, and recovery/readiness/M3 test contracts. The controller/UI is a separate audit; only the existing action enum and tests of its public recovery behavior were inspected here.
+
+## Main finding
+
+The pipeline has typed low-level failures but no `FailureKind` or `RecoveryAction` domain model. `ErrorRecoveryContext` is only `failedStage: String`, `error: Error`, `rawText: String?`, and `retryable: Bool` (`Sources/flowtype/Core/Pipeline/PipelineStage.swift:38`). The primary classification loss occurs at `ASRStage.swift:171`: terminal suspension after an unsuccessful provider chain uses a generic, retryable `ASRStageError.transcriptionFailed` except a first `RealtimeASRConfigurationError`. Even the preserved realtime configuration error is marked retryable. HTTP authentication/configuration/permanent rejection, unavailable engines, unsupported local model language, and transient timeouts therefore cannot reliably drive different recovery actions.
+
+M4 should add typed classification and a deterministic recovery policy at the stage boundary while retaining M3's complete-payload, cancellation, literal-preservation, and no-repeat-delivery guarantees. It does not need a new provider retry loop, transport replacement, model lifecycle rewrite, or persistence of raw audio.
+
+## Current contracts and existing types
+
+| Contract/type | Current shape | Source evidence | Implication for M4 |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `StagePayload` | empty; audio(samples, previewText); transcript; processed(text, raw); polished(text, raw) | `Core/Pipeline/PipelineStage.swift:6` | Audio and text provenance are already distinct; retain this distinction in recovery. |
+| `StageResult` | continue, skip, suspend(context), notice(string), complete | `Core/Pipeline/PipelineStage.swift:17` | Silence is deliberately a notice, optional polish deliberately continues, uncertain dispatch deliberately completes. Classification must not force all outcomes into suspend. |
+| `ErrorRecoveryContext` | String stage, arbitrary Error, optional String, Boolean retryability | `Core/Pipeline/PipelineStage.swift:38` | Cannot express permission vs config vs no-engine vs transient, or distinguish a new recording from retrying unchanged PCM. |
+| Owned execution | Reject canceled context before execution; replace result with complete if context canceled afterward; stage owns checks before side effects | `Core/Pipeline/PipelineStage.swift:68` | A classifier/action mapper cannot restore canceled/stale work or allow side effects merely because an error looks retryable. |
+| Existing UI command enum | `SessionController.ErrorAction`: retry(stage), copyRaw, copyResult, dismiss, openAccessibilitySettings, openMicrophoneSettings, openASRSettings, recheckReadiness, useAutomaticRouting | `Core/PipelineOrchestrator.swift:817` | Reuse/adapt this command vocabulary. No existing rerecord command. Avoid a parallel enum with identical command semantics unless the domain/UI boundary requires one. |
+| Readiness | `PermissionState`, `EngineReadiness`, `ReadinessIssue`, `ReadinessLevel` | `Core/Readiness/ReadinessSnapshot.swift:3`, `:7`, `:23`, `:39` | Reuse readiness issues/permission identity; do not infer no-engine from localized strings. |
+| Model provisioning | `ModelProvisionError` with typed categories and `isRetryable`; only network/stalled are retryable | `Services/Speech/ModelProvisioning/ModelProvisionError.swift:22`, `:37` | Already solves a separate operation's retry problem. Do not conflate download/load retry with ASR retry on captured audio. |
+| Diagnostics | `fallbackReason(for:)` returns timeout/network/unavailable/error/cancelled; reads typed errors, then NSError domain | `Services/Speech/ASRContract.swift:114` | Deliberately coarse and content-free; unsuitable as recovery policy. Keep metrics labels independent of user action classification. |
+
+In the remaining tables, paths beginning `Core/`, `Services/`, `Utilities/`, or `Testing/` are relative to `Sources/flowtype/`.
+
+## Stage trigger → current outcome → safe recovery
+
+### Recording
+
+| Trigger | Structured error/current result | Current payload/retryability | Safe recovery requirement/evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Microphone request denied before capture | `PermissionError.microphoneDenied`; suspend | rawText nil, retryable false | Open microphone settings + recheck + dismiss. Permission error is a repairable block, not same-stage retry. `RecordingStage.swift:51`; `PermissionHelper.swift:6`; action test `SelfTest.swift:553`. |
+| Permission revoked/raced between first permission request and `AudioRecorder.startRecording`'s request | `AudioRecorderError.permissionDenied`; thrown into generic recording catch/suspend | nil, false | Normalize both recording permission errors to the same microphone repair category. `AudioRecorder.swift:92`; `RecordingStage.swift:176`. Current test exercises `PermissionError`, not this second error type. |
+| PCM format or converter creation fails | `AudioRecorderError.formatCreationFailed`; generic recording catch/suspend | nil, false; accumulated audio discarded | Repair device/format and start a new capture. There is no complete ASR payload to retry. Restore default-device ownership before exit. `AudioRecorder.swift:177`, `:190`; `RecordingStage.swift:182`. |
+| Device stops producing taps for >5 seconds / disconnect freeze | callback sets frozen; spectrum ends; `AudioRecorderError.engineStartFailed`; suspend | nil, false; partial raw samples taken but not forwarded | Explain recording interrupted and rerecord after device repair. Never turn partial interrupted capture or preview into a transcript. `AudioRecorder.swift:213`, `:226`; `RecordingStage.swift:134`. |
+| `freshEngine.start()` throws | Caught inside `AudioRecorder` stream construction; spectrum is finished; freeze callback only for NSError domain `com.apple.coreaudio.avfaudio` | CoreAudio domain reaches engineStartFailed branch; other domains may return normal audio payload, commonly empty, then ASR empty-capture notice | Evidence gap: not every engine-start error is surfaced as a typed recording failure. Classifier alone cannot recover information the recorder swallows. Small follow-up seam could propagate typed start failure without exposing raw NSError strings. `AudioRecorder.swift:299`. |
+| Requested input device missing or default-input set fails | Logged; falls back to system default | no failure result | Do not invent a failure solely from a stale selected UID; current device fallback behavior is intentional. `AudioRecorder.swift:116`, `:162`, `:168`. |
+| Buffer allocation/conversion/empty channel failure | Tap callback drops bad buffer | no explicit error; heartbeat counts tap before conversion, so repeated conversion failure can lead to empty capture rather than freeze | Treat actual invalid saved samples distinctly from no recorded samples. `AudioRecorder.swift:252`, `:254`, `:272`; shape guard `:395`. A taxonomy cannot prove device health from heartbeat alone. |
+| Optional AppleSpeech preview unavailable/authorization/deadline | Preview start uses 3-second deadline and `try?`, substitutes finished stream | no recording failure | Preview failure must not block valid local/cloud ASR or become a microphone error. `RecordingStage.swift:92`; AppleSpeech preview authorization is separate (`AppleSpeechProvider.swift:129`). |
+| User stops recording | Recording task cancellation can mean stop; if context is still active, catch returns accumulated full audio + preview | continue audio, not a canceled failure | Preserve distinction between stop signal and session cancellation. `RecordingStage.swift:157`, `:164`, `:171`. |
+| Session canceled | Context inactive → complete; resources stopped/canceled/sealed under ownership | no recovery work | No settings, retry, copy, history, or late provider effects. `RecordingStage.swift:86`, `:164`, `:184`, `:194`; owned wrapper `PipelineStage.swift:75`. |
